{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>ויאמינו</b> Two times: ויאמינו בה' (and they believed in YHWH), ויאמינו אנשי נינוה באלהים (and the people of Nineveh believed in Elohim). As stated in the Midrash: not one remained among them — rather, one alone remained, namely Pharaoh, and he went to Nineveh and ruled there. And this is ויאמינו אנשי נינוה באלהים — remembered for what he saw in Egypt and at the Sea." "<b>ובמשה</b> Two times: ובמשה עבדו (and in Moses His servant), וידבר העם באלהים ובמשה (and the people spoke against Elohim and against Moses). To teach you: one who disputes his master is as one who disputes the Shekhinah, and one who believes the words of the Sages is as one who believes in the Shekhinah."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The midrashic logic: Pharaoh alone survived the Red Sea, later ruled Nineveh; his testimony prompted Nineveh's belief cited in Jonah 3:5."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:57.690902960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}